<unit id="4566d44d-44e5-4bf8-87b8-f29d4ecaaa03">
<notes>
<note appliesTo="source">line: 2</note>
<note appliesTo="source">prefix: # </note>
</notes>
<segment>
<source>Resource Monitor</source>
</segment>
</unit>
<unit id="e250d8eb-dbf6-4524-8b56-4c181d36e9f3">
<notes>
<note appliesTo="source">line: 4</note>
<note appliesTo="source">prefix: * </note>
</notes>
<segment>
<source>Authors: Alex Hall, Joseph Lee, Kefas Lungu, Beqa Gozalishvili, Tuukka Ojala, Ethin Probst, Kevin Derome and other NVDA contributors</source>
</segment>
</unit>
<unit id="4ba3b2ea-5e7e-4236-9e69-d99ce0e70168">
<notes>
<note appliesTo="source">line: 6</note>
</notes>
<segment>
<source>This add-on gives information about CPU load, memory usage and other resource usage information.</source>
</segment>
</unit>
<unit id="10cb3779-3d16-4d8b-a57e-36391bdd69e8">
<notes>
<note appliesTo="source">line: 8</note>
<note appliesTo="source">prefix: ## </note>
</notes>
<segment>
<source>Shortcuts</source>
</segment>
</unit>
<unit id="756f97fb-9153-48a2-83ca-6bc45c455fa1">
<notes>
<note appliesTo="source">line: 10</note>
</notes>
<segment>
<source>All commands support speech on demand mode.</source>
</segment>
</unit>
<unit id="7a14519c-52df-45b5-ab07-996d279b352f">
<notes>
<note appliesTo="source">line: 12</note>
<note appliesTo="source">prefix: * </note>
</notes>
<segment>
<source>NVDA+Shift+E: enters the Resource Monitor command layer.</source>
</segment>
</unit>
<unit id="6dce0d2e-0d7f-4831-94d3-e1ca82992dd0">
<notes>
<note appliesTo="source">line: 14</note>
</notes>
<segment>
<source>The following layer commands are available to obtain individual resource usage information:</source>
</segment>
</unit>
<unit id="724d95e3-5857-4026-9261-f589d39c1f2d">
<notes>
<note appliesTo="source">line: 16</note>
<note appliesTo="source">prefix: * </note>
</notes>
<segment>
<source>Space: overall resource usage information including used RAM (physical memory) and average processor load.</source>
</segment>
</unit>
<unit id="eb490626-6f38-4c38-96ab-93f36a15904e">
<notes>
<note appliesTo="source">line: 17</note>
<note appliesTo="source">prefix: * </note>
</notes>
<segment>
<source>C: CPU (average processor load and if multicore CPU's are present the load of each core)</source>
</segment>
</unit>
<unit id="6a1d0814-35cd-4b50-9120-c365ba32969a">
<notes>
<note appliesTo="source">line: 18</note>
<note appliesTo="source">prefix: * </note>
</notes>
<segment>
<source>D: disks (used and total space of the fixed (built-in), removable, and network drives)</source>
</segment>
</unit>
<unit id="50e4fc57-a99c-4a60-9274-466289eb29f2">
<notes>
<note appliesTo="source">line: 19</note>
<note appliesTo="source">prefix: * </note>
</notes>
<segment>
<source>G (unavailable in secure mode): graphics processing unit (GPU) information</source>
</segment>
</unit>
<unit id="6e5f3724-bb06-45d7-81d4-895793cc1923">
<notes>
<note appliesTo="source">line: 20</note>
<note appliesTo="source">prefix: * </note>
</notes>
<segment>
<source>Shift+G(unavailable in secure mode): GPU memory usage</source>
</segment>
</unit>
<unit id="c770b865-2c68-4200-b089-40d811c712b2">
<notes>
<note appliesTo="source">line: 21</note>
<note appliesTo="source">prefix: * </note>
</notes>
<segment>
<source>M: memory (used and total space for both physical and virtual RAM (NVDA+Shift+5 is an alternative to NVDA+Shift+2 when the latter keyboard combination cannot be performed))</source>
</segment>
</unit>
<unit id="3398c766-51e9-4613-9d15-74015e1a0bf7">
<notes>
<note appliesTo="source">line: 22</note>
<note appliesTo="source">prefix: * </note>
</notes>
<segment>
<source>O: operating system (Windows version, CPU architecture, and exact build number (build.revision))</source>
</segment>
</unit>
<unit id="efa513cd-d061-4b49-a66c-97ec5140a91d">
<notes>
<note appliesTo="source">line: 23</note>
<note appliesTo="source">prefix: * </note>
</notes>
<segment>
<source>U: system uptime</source>
</segment>
</unit>
<unit id="956ebd51-65d0-4420-bfe0-e480e0d3b8ec">
<notes>
<note appliesTo="source">line: 24</note>
<note appliesTo="source">prefix: * </note>
</notes>
<segment>
<source>W: wi-fi (network name (SSID), signal strength, security mode, or no SSID if there is none available)</source>
</segment>
</unit>
<unit id="64400d14-bf51-48c5-8d5b-24f402f10805">
<notes>
<note appliesTo="source">line: 26</note>
</notes>
<segment>
<source>Resource commands keep the layer active so they can be repeated. Press Escape to exit the layer; an unmapped key exits and is passed through the active application.</source>
</segment>
</unit>
<unit id="dc6a849c-dc3c-43e1-9d9b-17e3aa1177ee">
<notes>
<note appliesTo="source">line: 28</note>
</notes>
<segment>
<source>For limited backward compatibility, the previous NVDA+Shift+1 through NVDA+Shift+7 resource shortcuts remain available:</source>
</segment>
</unit>
<unit id="d01e5bb5-e2c5-4984-9a5e-75a8656e5b34">
<notes>
<note appliesTo="source">line: 30</note>
<note appliesTo="source">prefix: * </note>
</notes>
<segment>
<source>NVDA+Shift+1: CPU</source>
</segment>
</unit>
<unit id="e6882ad3-cf8b-4850-96ce-c94ec64d2d82">
<notes>
<note appliesTo="source">line: 31</note>
<note appliesTo="source">prefix: * </note>
</notes>
<segment>
<source>NVDA+Shift+2/5: memory</source>
</segment>
</unit>
<unit id="c75947e5-b289-4072-9d34-638be5b92815">
<notes>
<note appliesTo="source">line: 32</note>
<note appliesTo="source">prefix: * </note>
</notes>
<segment>
<source>NVDA+Shift+3: disks</source>
</segment>
</unit>
<unit id="8d7c7925-6be9-475d-bd22-24db68fdc143">
<notes>
<note appliesTo="source">line: 33</note>
<note appliesTo="source">prefix: * </note>
</notes>
<segment>
<source>NVDA+Shift+4: wi-fi</source>
</segment>
</unit>
<unit id="588f5c4c-5f37-4376-acfb-73f8364f9ea6">
<notes>
<note appliesTo="source">line: 34</note>
<note appliesTo="source">prefix: * </note>
</notes>
<segment>
<source>NVDA+Shift+6: operating system</source>
</segment>
</unit>
<unit id="763fe702-d357-447b-8999-0da9288a1034">
<notes>
<note appliesTo="source">line: 35</note>
<note appliesTo="source">prefix: * </note>
</notes>
<segment>
<source>NVDA+Shift+7: system uptime</source>
</segment>
</unit>
<unit id="17db2052-331b-4eb2-9524-28b4f94dfb3a">
<notes>
<note appliesTo="source">line: 37</note>
</notes>
<segment>
<source>You can change these gestures via the input gestures dialog.</source>
</segment>
</unit>
<unit id="cf9d1f4c-49a9-44c6-b161-ecfd913e64f6">
<notes>
<note appliesTo="source">line: 39</note>
<note appliesTo="source">prefix: ## </note>
</notes>
<segment>
<source>Usage notes</source>
</segment>
</unit>
<unit id="6afdbb36-1fa8-4498-99e0-3af26ac88091">
<notes>
<note appliesTo="source">line: 41</note>
</notes>
<segment>
<source>This add-on does not replace task manager and other system information programs for Windows. Also note the following:</source>
</segment>
</unit>
<unit id="be5a90cc-97c4-4f1d-a612-7cdea631f49a">
<notes>
<note appliesTo="source">line: 43</note>
<note appliesTo="source">prefix: * </note>
</notes>
<segment>
<source>Pressing resource commands twice will copy resource usage information to the clipboard.</source>
</segment>
</unit>
<unit id="70ea07e4-d172-4dc7-aa11-970495a5c25e">
<notes>
<note appliesTo="source">line: 44</note>
<note appliesTo="source">prefix: * </note>
</notes>
<segment>
<source>Resource information cannot be copied to the clipboard if running the add-on in secure screens.</source>
</segment>
</unit>
<unit id="f30cb84e-93b4-4c9e-b1e7-ea10a41b7434">
<notes>
<note appliesTo="source">line: 45</note>
<note appliesTo="source">prefix: * </note>
</notes>
<segment>
<source>CPU usage is given for logical processors, not physical cores. This is noticeable for processors with Hyper-Threading where number of CPU's is twice the number of CPU cores. On some newer computers, not all CPU cores will have hyper-threading enabled.</source>
</segment>
</unit>
<unit id="e7463f56-ef68-4bc5-b6de-b4a53feff8e7">
<notes>
<note appliesTo="source">line: 46</note>
<note appliesTo="source">prefix: * </note>
</notes>
<segment>
<source>If there is heavy disk activity such as copying large files or while locating network drives, there might be delays when obtaining disk usage information.</source>
</segment>
</unit>
<unit id="843f5230-c7a3-47e4-94f9-e20d98046a36">
<notes>
<note appliesTo="source">line: 47</note>
<note appliesTo="source">prefix: * </note>
</notes>
<segment>
<source>GPU information is given for Nvidia GPU's.</source>
</segment>
</unit>
<unit id="cb5afef8-535b-45b2-bc60-64b07663bed7">
<notes>
<note appliesTo="source">line: 48</note>
<note appliesTo="source">prefix: * </note>
</notes>
<segment>
<source>When announcing processor architecture information as part of Windows version reporting, "AMD64" refer to 64-bit (x64) Intel and AMD processors. This information does not refer to the name of the actual processor in use.</source>
</segment>
</unit>
<unit id="2526a96e-9263-4d2b-acf3-adf0ebf773e0">
<notes>
<note appliesTo="source">line: 49</note>
<note appliesTo="source">prefix: * </note>
</notes>
<segment>
<source>Installing the add-on on Windows 10/11 LTSC is not supported.</source>
</segment>
</unit>
<unit id="cede3681-25e1-4335-adad-b188883c418e">
<notes>
<note appliesTo="source">line: 51</note>
</notes>
<segment>
<source>For a list of changes made between each add-on releases, refer to [changelogs for add-on releases][1] document.</source>
</segment>
</unit>
<unit id="32d59eb2-cc6d-4498-8a04-ed6e06dbe82e">
<notes>
<note appliesTo="source">line: 53</note>
</notes>
<segment>
<source>[1]: https://github.com/kefaslungu/resourceMonitor/blob/main/changes.md</source>
</segment>
</unit>
